{"seq":20,"trial_id":"shared-bot-scope-2026-11/hermes-opus-gbrain-refused-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-14T13:28:43.266Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"dd3d3326795afbdc5ff5a50e09d36ae19c90036be5418062906c5160c924bbe7","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared files. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025: gatehouse kiosk SMS bay assignments weren't reaching drivers at Dock Doors 14-18 in the Eau Claire yard. Support patched it the same evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the 04:00 shift got through. There's also a follow-up item to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it: gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nI left some numbers out on purpose. #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in Moss's Central handoffs digest are for Marrow accounts, not QFL. Moss's 2025-09-14 North pipeline digest and 2026-03-23 renewal check-in mention QFL but don't give any ticket numbers. One more thing: the cheat sheet warns that Quarendon Freightways is a different company and not a customer, so keep the two apart in the notes. I couldn't check the knowledge brain (it refused my access), so this list only covers Moss's notes in the shared files."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
